---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const lastUpdated = '23 April 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy — The Breaking Dad"
  description="Privacy policy for thebreakingdad.co.uk — how we collect, use, and protect your data."
  noindex={false}
>
  <div class="static-page">
    <div class="container--narrow">

      <nav class="static-page__breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true"> / </span>
        <span aria-current="page">Privacy policy</span>
      </nav>

      <h1 class="static-page__title">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="static-page__updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="prose">

        <p>
          This privacy policy explains how The Breaking Dad (<strong>thebreakingdad.co.uk</strong>),
          operated by Dan Betts, collects, uses, and protects any information when you use this website.
          This site is based in the United Kingdom and complies with the UK GDPR and the Data Protection Act 2018.
        </p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          The Breaking Dad is a personal blog operated by Dan Betts, based in Hampshire, UK.
          For data protection queries, contact: <a href="mailto:dan@thebreakingdad.co.uk">dan@thebreakingdad.co.uk</a>
        </p>

        <h2>What data we collect</h2>
        <p>
          This is a static website with no login, no comments, and no newsletter (yet).
          We collect minimal data:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Server logs.</strong> Like most websites, our hosting infrastructure
            (Cloudflare) automatically records basic request data: IP addresses, browser type,
            pages visited, and referrer URLs. Cloudflare's privacy policy governs this data.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare Web Analytics.</strong> Cookieless, edge-collected pageview data
            (URL, referrer, country, device class). No personal data, no tracking across sites,
            no consent banner needed. We use it for a ground-truth traffic baseline.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics 4 (GA4).</strong> Once you accept the cookie banner, GA4
            sets cookies and records anonymised event data so we can understand which articles
            help most. If you decline (or ignore the banner), GA4 stays in default-deny mode and
            doesn't set cookies or record identifiable data on you. You can change your choice
            anytime: see "Managing your consent" below.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Contact information.</strong> If you email us or contact us via Instagram,
            we receive your name and contact details as part of that interaction.
            We only use this to respond to you and do not add you to any mailing list.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Affiliate link clicks.</strong> When you click an affiliate link on this site,
            the retailer or affiliate network may set cookies and collect data about your visit.
            We do not control this data. See our <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a>
            for more detail on which networks we use.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          This site sets first-party cookies only when you accept the cookie banner. The cookies
          come from Google Analytics 4 (typically <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_&lt;ID&gt;</code>)
          and are used to understand aggregate site usage. We don't use them for advertising or
          cross-site tracking.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you decline the banner (or ignore it), no first-party cookies are set. Third-party
          services (affiliate networks, embedded videos when present) may set their own cookies
          when you interact with them.
        </p>

        <h2>Managing your consent</h2>
        <p>
          You can change your analytics consent at any time. The simplest way: clear this site's
          site data (browser settings → Privacy → clear data for thebreakingdad.co.uk), then
          reload the site — the consent banner will reappear and you can pick again.
        </p>
        <p>
          You can also block analytics entirely using a privacy-focused browser extension or your
          browser's built-in tracking protection. We respect that choice.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            <strong>Cloudflare</strong>: hosting, CDN, and cookieless Web Analytics. Processes
            request data and pageview metadata as described above.
            <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cloudflare privacy policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Google Analytics 4 (Google LLC)</strong>: site usage analytics, only after
            you accept the cookie banner. Google may transfer data to the US under their standard
            contractual clauses.
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google privacy policy</a>.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Affiliate networks</strong>: when applicable. See our
            <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> for details of which networks
            we work with.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong>Instagram / Meta</strong>: we link to our Instagram profile. If you visit
            Instagram, Meta's privacy policy applies.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Your rights under UK GDPR</h2>
        <p>
          You have the right to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Access the personal data we hold about you</li>
          <li>Request correction of inaccurate data</li>
          <li>Request erasure of your data (the "right to be forgotten")</li>
          <li>Object to processing of your data</li>
          <li>Request restriction of processing</li>
          <li>Data portability</li>
          <li>Lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ICO) at <a href="https://ico.org.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ico.org.uk</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these rights, email:
          <a href="mailto:dan@thebreakingdad.co.uk">dan@thebreakingdad.co.uk</a>
        </p>

        <h2>Data retention</h2>
        <p>
          We retain server log data only as long as required by Cloudflare's standard retention
          policy. Contact correspondence is retained until no longer needed for the purpose of
          the original communication.
        </p>

        <h2>External links</h2>
        <p>
          This website contains links to external sites. We are not responsible for the privacy
          practices of those sites and encourage you to read their privacy policies.
        </p>

        <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          This website is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
          personal data from children.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          We may update this privacy policy from time to time. The "last updated" date at the
          top of this page will reflect any changes. Continued use of the site after changes
          constitutes acceptance of the revised policy.
        </p>

      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .static-page {
    padding-block: 2rem 5rem;
  }

  .static-page__breadcrumb {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.8125rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }

  .static-page__breadcrumb a {
    color: var(--color-muted);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .static-page__breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .static-page__title {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: clamp(1.875rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .static-page__updated {
    font-family: var(--font-sans);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    margin: 0 0 2rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
